  "executive_briefing": "The mid-2026 tax environment is characterized by a definitive retreat from the multilateral, cooperative fiscal models of the early 2020s toward sovereign, competitive tax policies. Pillar Two of the OECD framework faces significant headwinds as nations prioritize local tax credits and targeted incentive structures over global compliance. Simultaneously, the normalization of high-frequency, unilateral tariff deployments as a primary diplomatic tool has created extreme uncertainty for global supply chains. At the operational level, digital transformation is the only area of sustained consensus, with mandatory, structured e-invoicing frameworks becoming the global baseline for tax transparency and enforcement.",
